 2. 🤖 AI model hype goes wild 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Stock: Getty Images The online chatter about new AI models is starting to resemble the hype over the next Taylor Swift album or where LeBron James might end his career, Axios' Herb Scribner and Andrew Kay write. 

 🦁 The frenzy might start with a post from "leo," a reliable AI leaker with more than 34,000 followers.

 Leo's posts can get picked up by Kim "Chubby" Isenberg, the Superintelligence editor-in-chief with more than 130,000 followers who's quick to aggregate AI chatter. 🤔 An AI writer, investor or CEO might throw in some speculation based on Chubby's post.

 The timeline then becomes a free-flowing river of rumors, information and theories. Reality check: As Swifties know all too well, the rumor mill is noisy and often wrong.

